From cef3757e4d7cf237123ca0b9dee5d294521cb6fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:28:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] usb: typec: add Silicon Mitus SM5714 Type-C CC driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The SM5714 is a combo PMIC integrating a charger, a fuel gauge and a
Type-C/USB block. Add a driver for its Type-C CC detection block, found on
Samsung phones such as the Galaxy A52 (SM7125).

The driver reacts to CC attach and detach interrupts: it switches the USB
controller between device and host role through a USB role switch, and
enables the VBUS regulator while in host role. USB Power Delivery is not
handled. The CC interrupt is masked across system sleep because the level
line can otherwise re-fire before the parent I2C controller has resumed.

No public datasheet is available; the register layout is taken from the
Samsung downstream driver.

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
